### 1. Navigate to the Project Folder                                      
                                                                             
  Because the folder name contains spaces and a colon (:), wrap the path in  
  quotes in your terminal:                                                   
                                                                             
    cd "/Users/hasithadhananjaya/Desktop/Enterprise LAN:WLAN Design &        
    Subnetting Simulation "                                                  
  ──────                                                                     
  ### 2. Install Dependencies                                                
                                                                             
  If you ever clone or copy the project to a new machine or pull updates:    
                                                                             
    npm install                                                              
  ──────                                                                     
  ### 3. Start the Development Server                                        
                                                                             
  Starts the local development server with hot module replacement (HMR):     
                                                                             
    npm run dev                                                              
                                                                             
  │ Direct binary alternative (if needed):                                   
  │                                                                          
  │   node ./node_modules/vite/bin/vite.js                                   
                                                                             
  Then open your browser to http://localhost:3000 (or run open               
  http://localhost:3000 on macOS).                                           
  ──────                                                                     
  ### 4. Build for Production                                                
                                                                             
  Type-checks TypeScript and compiles the optimized production bundle into   
  the dist/ folder:                                                          
                                                                             
    npm run build                                                            
  ──────                                                                     
  ### 5. Preview the Production Build                                        
                                                                             
  Locally tests and serves the production build created in dist/:            
                                                                             
    npm run preview                                                          
  ──────                                                                     
  ### 6. Useful Optional Flags                                               
                                                                             
  • Expose to Local Network (accessible from other devices / tablets on your 
  Wi-Fi):                                                                    
    npm run dev -- --host                                                    
                                                                             
  • Run on a Custom Port (e.g. port 8080):                                   
    npm run dev -- --port 8080                                               
                                                                             
  • Automatically Open Browser on Start:                                     
    npm run dev -- --open                                                    
                         